{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And we will be slaves to Pharaoh.</b> They were precise to say, for their servitude is to Pharaoh and not to Yosef." "<b>Further,</b> they may intend to say in the manner of what I explained above, that he acquired them only to specify the labor of the land. Therefore they said, ״וְהָיִינוּ עֲבָדִים״ — the servitude in its entirety is to Pharaoh, and not to the labor of the land alone. Or perhaps it is for this reason that the Egyptians intended when they spoke with Pharaoh concerning Israel and said (Exodus 1:9): ״הִנֵּה עַם בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל רַב וְגוֹ׳ מִמֶּנּוּ״ — meaning, for he has no name of servitude as they all were slaves to Pharaoh."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:38.022240318Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}